course: dictionary
lesson: 12010
title: Cheerleader
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cheerleader is a person who dances, shouts chants and does jumps to cheer on a sports team and the crowd. «The cheerleaders jumped and shouted when the home team scored.» The sentence tells you what they do: they jump, shout and cheer. That is the first meaning.
explain: The word can also mean anyone who strongly supports and encourages a person or an idea. «My grandma was my cheerleader at every race.» Grandma was not dancing or jumping. She was always there to cheer me on and help me keep going.
explain: Check the clues around the word. Ask: is this about a sports game, or about someone who helps and encourages a person? If you swap in your meaning and the sentence still makes sense, you are probably right.
fact: A cheerleader cheers for a team, often at school football and basketball games.
fact: Cheerleaders use chants, dances and jumps to encourage the team and the crowd.
fact: Cheerleading is also a competitive sport, with stunts and tumbling.
fact: Cheerleading squad means the group of cheerleaders, and a cheerleader uniform is what they wear.
fact: «My biggest cheerleader» means the person who always encourages me.
exercise: «The cheerleaders jumped and shouted for the home team.» What are the cheerleaders doing? | Selling tickets | *Encouraging the team with chants and jumps | Cleaning the stands | Playing in goal
exercise: Mia says, «My best friend is my biggest cheerleader.» What does this mean? | Her friend is the tallest in the class | *Her friend always encourages her | Her friend shouts at her during games | Her friend plays basketball for the school
exercise: «The cheerleaders wore bright red uniforms and waved pom-poms.» Find and copy the word for the clothes they wore. | bright | game | *uniforms | waved
test: What is a cheerleader at a sports game? | The referee who blows the whistle | *A person who dances, chants and jumps to support a team | The player who scores the goals
test: «Ben is his sister's cheerleader. He always tells her she can do it.» What does cheerleader mean here? | A referee | *Someone who strongly supports and encourages her | A person who sings in a choir | A team captain
exam: «Grandma was my cheerleader at every race.» What does cheerleader mean in this sentence? | The judge who checks the times | A runner in the race | *Someone who always supports and encourages me | A person who sells drinks at the track
